---
title: "6 · Approval"
description: Submit a contract for approval, and approve or return it.
sidebar:
  order: 7
  label: "6 · Approval"
---

**Who:** the person in charge submits; the department lead of the person in charge approves.

## Submit

Write a **Note to the approver (optional)** if it helps the approver, and select **Submit for approval**. The contract waits for approval when either of these applies:

- the total discount is above the firm's threshold (10% by default);
- the draft was edited by hand.

Otherwise the contract is ready to send at once: the same button reads **Continue to signing** and the contract moves to step 4.

After submitting, the submitter sees who the contract is waiting for and why. The submitter can select **Withdraw and edit**, or send the approver a reminder with **Remind** and the approver's name (at most once an hour).

{% screenshot id="crm/approval-submitter" caption="What the submitter sees." /%}

## Approve

The approver sees a red count on **Opportunity** in the navigation. The approver opens the contract and checks each line against the catalog price in the **Catalog**, **Agreed** and **Difference** columns. For an edited draft, **Open edited draft** and **Compare with generated draft** show what was changed.

Then select **Approve**, or write a comment and select **Return to draft**. A comment is required to return the contract.

{% screenshot id="crm/approval-approver" caption="What the approver sees: the reason, the note and the difference on each line." /%}

{% aside type="note" title="No self-approval" %}
When the department lead submits the contract, a tenant admin approves it. In the examples, Demo Manager (the department lead) submits, and Demo Accountant (a tenant admin) approves.
{% /aside %}
